{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the man knew.</b> Already before the matter above — before he sinned and was banished from the Garden of Eden — and likewise the pregnancy and the birth. For if it were written וַיֵּדַע אָדָם, it would sound as though after he was banished he had sons." "<b>Cain.</b> After the word קָנִיתִי." "<b>Et YHWH.</b> Like 'with YHWH' — when He created me and my husband, He alone created us, but in this we are partners with Him (Niddah 31)." "<b>Et Cain et his brother et Abel.</b> Three instances of אֶת are pluralative; they teach that a twin was born with Cain, and with Abel two were born — therefore it says וַתֹּסֶף (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:28.829952411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}